**Finding**: `KanbanBoard.tsx` has no `onDragCancel` handler on `<DndContext>`. When the user presses Escape to cancel a keyboard drag, `activeItem` state (which drives the `DragOverlay`) is never cleared, leaving the ghost card/lane floating indefinitely.

**Code to check** (KanbanBoard.tsx):
```tsx
const handleDragEnd = ({ active, over }: DragEndEvent) => {
  setActiveItem(null)          // clears on successful end
  activeRef.current = null
  if (!over || active.id === over.id) return
  // ...
}

// announcements object handles onDragCancel string only
const announcements = {
  onDragStart: ...,
  onDragOver: ...,
  onDragEnd: ...,
  onDragCancel: ({ active }: DragStartEvent) => `Move cancelled for ${active.id}.`,
}

return (
  <>
    <DndContext
      sensors={sensors}
      collisionDetection={closestCenter}
      onDragStart={handleDragStart}
      onDragEnd={handleDragEnd}
      // NO onDragCancel prop here
      accessibility={{ announcements }}
    >
      <SortableContext ...>
        {sortedLanes.map((lane) => <Lane ... />)}
      </SortableContext>
      <DragOverlay>
        {activeItem?.type === 'card' && <CardDragPreview card={activeItem.item} />}
