**dnd-kit behavior**: In dnd-kit, `onDragCancel` fires when the user presses Escape or the drag is cancelled for other reasons. It is a SEPARATE event from `onDragEnd`. `handleDragEnd` does NOT fire on Escape — only `onDragCancel` fires. Without an `onDragCancel` handler that calls `setActiveItem(null)`, the `DragOverlay` will continue to render the active item.

